WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.830
A GitHub profile is already proof of what someone can do. Almost nobody reads it that way.

2
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.440
Sign in with GitHub. That is the entire setup.

3
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.630
Repositories import from one or more GitHub accounts, public or private.

4
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:26.460
Six phases analyse each repository. Every phase records its own status and its own error.

5
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:32.110
Nothing is written about a repository until it has been analysed.

6
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.880
Select the analysed repositories and generate. The developer writes nothing.

7
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.200
One failing agent costs one section of the portfolio, not the whole run.

8
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:54.640
Framework detection writes a mandatory override into the prompt. The model phrases the finding; it does not determine it.

9
00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:00.920
The headline and summary are generated from the code, not typed by the developer.

10
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:10.320
Every figure is counted from the repository at commit 966e5d69, and can be re-derived.

11
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.660
Nothing covers the pipeline, the agents or the endpoints. The record says so itself.

12
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.940
Every claim on the page is pinned to a commit you can open.
